$)

  $c X_ $.

  $( Extend class notation to include infinite Cartesian products. $)
  cixp $a class X_ x e. A B $.

  ${
    $d f x $.  $d f A $.  $d f B $.
    $( Definition of infinite Cartesian product of [Enderton] p. 54.  Enderton
       uses a bold "X" with ` x e. A ` written underneath or as a subscript,
       as does Stoll p. 47.  Some books use a capital pi, but we will reserve
       that notation for products of numbers.  Usually ` B ` represents a
       class expression containing ` x ` free and thus can be thought of
       as ` B ( x ) ` .  Normally, ` x ` is not free in ` A ` , although this
       is not a requirement of the definition. $)
    df-ixp $a |- X_ x e. A B =
                 { f | ( f Fn A /\ A. x e. A ( f ` x ) e. B ) } $.
  $}

  ${
    $d f A $.  $d f B $.  $d f x F $.
    $( Membership in an infinite Cartesian product.  See ~ df-ixp for
       discussion of the notation. $)
