    $( The image of a group ` G ` under a group homomorphism ` F ` is a group,
       and furthermore is Abelian if ` G ` is Abelian.  This is a stronger
       result than that usually found in the literature, since the target of
       the homomorphism (operator ` O ` in our model) need not have any of the
       properties of a group as a prerequisite.  (Contributed by Paul Chapman,
       25-Apr-2008.) $)
