       (i.e. the vectors, with the operation of vector addition) accompanied
       by a scalar multiplication operation on the field of complex numbers.
       The variable ` W ` was chosen because ` V ` is already used for the
       universal class. $)
    vci $p |- ( W e. CVec ->
              ( G e. Abel /\
         S :  ( CC X. X ) --> X /\ A. x e. X ( ( 1 S x ) = x /\
       A. y e. CC ( A. z e. X ( y S ( x G z ) ) = ( ( y S x ) G ( y S z ) )
         /\ A. z e. CC ( ( ( y + z ) S x ) = ( ( y S x ) G ( z S x ) ) /\
           ( ( y x. z ) S x ) = ( y S ( z S x ) ) ) ) ) ) ) $=
      ( vg vs cvc wcel cv cabl cc crn cxp wf c1 co wceq wral caddc cmul wa w3a
      copab df-vc eleq2i c1st cfv wb eqeq2i eleq1 rneq syl6eqr xpeq2 feq2 syl
      feq3 bitrd opreq opreq2d eqeq12d raleq12d eqeq2d anbi1d ralbidv anbi12d
      anbi2d 3anbi123d sylbir c2nd feq1 eqeq1d opreq12d eqtrd 3anbi23d elopabi
      sylbi ) FMNFKOZPNZQWCRZSZWELOZTZUAAOZWGUBZWIUCZBOZWICOZWCUBZWGUBZWLWIWGUB
      ZWLWMWGUBZWCUBZUCZCWEUDZWLWMUEUBZWIWGUBZWPWMWIWGUBZWCUBZUCZWLWMUFUBZWIWGU
