  $c SubCat $.
  $( Extend class notation with a function returning all the subcategories of
     a given category. $)
  csubc $a class SubCat $.

  ${ $d x y a $.
    $( ` ( SubCat `` x ) ` is the set of all the subcategories of the
       category ` x ` . All the objects and all the morphisms of the subcategory
       belong to the supercategory. The identity of an object, the domain and
       the codomain of a morphism are the same in the subcategory and the
       supercategory. The composition of the subcategory is a restriction of
       the composition of the supercategory. $)
  df-subc $a |- SubCat = { <. x , y >. | ( x e. Cat /\ y = { a e. Cat | (
    ( id_ ` a ) (_ ( id_ ` x ) /\ ( ( dom_ ` a ) (_ ( dom_ ` x )
    /\ ( cod_ ` a ) (_ ( cod_ ` x ) ) /\  ( o_ ` a ) (_ ( o_ ` x ) ) } ) }  $.
  $}

